+## Product trajectory view
+
+The existing chat Thread keeps its Message, Reasoning, Tool, Plan,
+Verification, Sources, and Composer rendering. A per-conversation
+`Conversation / Trajectory` switch mounts the browser-only
+`@perix/event-ui` package directly in the same page; the integration does not
+copy the DSH components, use an iframe, or maintain a Nexent-specific
+trajectory renderer. The selected view is restored independently for each
+conversation after a reload.
+
+The frontend retrieves every trajectory page through the authenticated Nexent
+endpoint and passes the common Event v0 records to `TrajectoryViewer`. During
+an active run it polls incrementally from the last sequence number. Empty,
+missing, unavailable, and malformed responses remain distinct user-visible
+states. The fork action defaults to the latest completed `turn/end` boundary,
+creates the corresponding Nexent child conversation, and navigates directly to
+its inherited trajectory view.
+
+The frontend packages are committed as reproducible tarballs under
+`frontend/vendor/` and were packed from Perix runtime data commit
+`3a1f931ddcd7f94944789a195536208405b7182d`:
+
+```text
+perix-event-sdk-0.1.0.tgz  sha256 bb711c641314026522f2e54fe14e219411727c7192554275d8ed129ef3e1caed
+perix-event-ui-0.1.0.tgz   sha256 5ef17461ff7f8f0f5175687496140a2aa3bcd8ad831b7301b60863e94c7f6da1
+```
+
 ## Verification
 
 Install both optional test groups and run the focused acceptance suite:
@@ -141,3 +168,18 @@ runner. The acceptance test launches fresh Python processes from outside the
 repository root, verifies that `perix_event` resolves from `site-packages`,
 executes a real `CoreAgent` tool call, resumes the parent Session, forks it, and
 independently continues the child.
+
+Run the frontend trajectory and regression checks from `frontend/`:
+
+```bash
+pnpm test
+pnpm exec tsc --noEmit --incremental false
+pnpm build
+```
+
+`pnpm test` includes pagination, response validation, fork URL construction,
+completed-turn boundary selection, per-conversation view persistence, and the
+existing chat viewport/date/load-policy tests. Browser acceptance additionally
+uses the committed R33 parent/child Event fixture to verify the unchanged chat,
+toolbar, timeline, Turn/Step/Tool rows, search, global folding, event detail,
+reload persistence, and child navigation.
